I'm not sure this is relevant to the problem, but I recall a problem
with the DECwindows server provided with Ultrix4.0.  Contrary to what the
MIT server does, it ignores any font aliases when the target font name
is not already known at that point in the font path.
In the case above, any font aliases in the fonts/devwin/100dpi directory
that refer to fonts found in the fonts/MIT directory will not take effect.
You'd have to switch the order of directories.  
