	I can't explain the full behaviour, but perhaps the following will
allow you a work-around.  I have no trouble with the MIT fonts under 4.1/4.2
on a 5000/200.  /usr/lib/X11/fonts/MIT/fonts.dir contains lines like:
	8x13.pcf	8x13
	8x13bold.pcf	8x13bold
/usr/lib/X11/fonts/MIT/fonts.alias contains lines like:
	vtbold		8x13bold

The longest description of fontpath behaviour (not that I understand it all ;-)
is in the Ultrix release notes section 4.3.  Note that you should be able to
get what you want by placing the single line "FILE_NAMES_ALIASES" in file
fonts.aliases.  Also note that there is a dxmkfontdir which for all I know may
do things differently than the MIT mkfontdir.  I don't recall running either
of them; I just took the files as they came on the distribution tape.

