In article <ROCKER.91Jul17232557@bucsf.bu.edu>, rocker@bucsf.bu.edu (The Long Haired One) writes:
> 
> I've got an old PDP-11/23, its in a half-height cabinet, and was wondering
> if the cabinet has a special name. Also if someone can explain what a BA123
> and a BA23 cabinet are also. I'd appreciate the info.

  The PDP-11/23 in a H9642 cabinet generally bears the model "11T23", and
was sold as a packaged system with (usually) RL02 disk drives.

  The BA23 is a small floor-standing box (looks like one of those portable
oil-filled radiators 8-) which houses 8 quad slots and has 2 mounting slots
for full-height 5.25" devices (disks, tapes, etc). It is a wonderful system
from the user's point of view, but can be hard to work on when you get a lot
of cards in it. Also, changing disks is complicated by the need for near-
complete disassembly of the cabinet.

  The BA123 is a larger cabinet with 13 quad slots, 5 slots for full-height
5.25" devices, twice the power, and lots more spots for mounting cabinet
kits. It features casters for easy movement and much easier access to the
cards and disk devices.

  BA23's are available used from various vendors for about $300, and BA123's
for about $1000.

