To transfer files between a PDP11 running RT11 and a VAX running VMS is
quite simple. If you like to do it over a communication link there are
several options. You can use VTCOM from the PDP to the VAX if you want
to transfer ASCII-files. This could not be done with the BASELINE or
SINGLE JOB monitor in the PDP. You have to have F/B or XM (I think..). 
Most RT11 machines today run XM. You also need a serial line extra (DLV11 
will do nicely and could be had for free. People toss them at you! :) ).
If you do not like VTCOM there is always KERMIT. Works fine with RT11.
You need PASCAL on your RT11 machine to compile it. Have not seen KERMIT for
RT11 written in Fortran 77 or IV or MACRO.
Then you can use DECNET of course. I think that DECNET/RT11 is a layered
product. That is MORE DINERO TO DIGITAL.....
If you have any removable magnetic media in common you can use it for transfer.
The VAX/VMSen can read RT11 format (with the EXCHANGE utility).
Heck, you can even do an octal dump, take it out on a huge printer and
force YOUR secretary to hack it in for you in TECO and then dehex it if
you like. More known as the governement techique....
So, friend, it is GOOD news if you have a PDP with RT11 and a VAX/VMS and
you wanna transfer data between them.
/L. Persson, Harlosa PD computer centre.
(We supply free bytes and computing power from the good old days. :) )


