	I have already replied directly to Malcolm about this, but since it
has generated more net traffic, I will post here. 

	I have a utility program (actually a minor enhancement of 'ansitape')
which will read RT11 format (& RT11 BUP format) magtapes properly (no fudges)
on unix. Directories, individual files etc. Vanilla ansitape will accept
RT11 tapes, but messes up data due to some errors in RT11 ansii headers. My
version identifies RT11 tapes & reacts accordingly.

	If anyone wants it, please contact me directly. It's simple &
fast to transfer data via magtapes.

	One thing I have not yet got around to writing is a a 'c' utility
which will delve into RT11 device image files to get individual files out.
This is necessary for V5.5 BUP tapes which enclose all saved files in
device images. I've started writing it, but haven't had time to finish.
Anyone out there done done this?


