In article <NEPTUNE.91Jul3100759@fenchurch.mit.edu> neptune@fenchurch.mit.edu writes:
> 
> I am converting from a 4.3BSD system to Ultrix 4.1.  I am currently
> using a non-HDB uucp with subdirectories, I don't remember where it
> came from.  I would like some opinions and comments on Ultrix UUCP so
> that I can decide if I need to go hunting for another UUCP
> implementation or if I can use the Ultrix one.
> 
> I need a UUCP that is capable of handling 30+ polling sites and
> ~10 tcp/uucp sites, all running different versions of UUCP ranging
> from HDB to DECUS to UUPC.  I'd be particularly interested in hearing
> from people who have used Ultrix UUCP with other flavors of UUCP such
> as these.
> 

The ultrix uucp is based on a ~4.2 BSD UUCP with modifications.  I supports
subdirectories, but the scheme is not exactly the same as the BSD 4.3*
scheme.  It *DOES NOT* support TCP connections.

If you want to install one of the BSD versions, you wil probably want to
modify the "dialers" you plan to use to support Ultrix serial line sharing,
though you may be able to use the BSD utility.

