In article <1991Jul3.074100.19898@menudo.uh.edu> wjin@sun2.cs.uh.edu (Woochang Jin) writes:
> Our department bought 15 DEC3100 workstations from DEC, each of which has
> about 600 M bytes disk space. Unfortunately, some of them are Ultrix 3.1D
> others are Ultrix 4.0 and one or two has Ultrix 4.1.   
> 
> Since we have a permission to use/copy
> any software on those mahines on other DEC3100's,  we would like to
> make all the DEC3100's have Ultrix 4.1.
> Currently, all the machines are connected on NFS and working.
> Is there a smooth and easy way to upgrade 3.1 and 4.0 to 4.1 ?

Not really.  I'd suggest you start with Ultrix 4.2 and do nice clean install
on one of the machines.  If people haven't been too creative, you can then
copy root/user/var to each of the other machines and make appropriate local
changes to each.

Also, if the machines are diskless or near diskless systems, it's worth the
effort to have them mount a shared (read-only) /usr filesystem on the server
system.  I haven't don't this with 4.2 yet, but it only required a little
fiddling under 3.1 - copying a few programs from /usr to /bin and changing
the order a few operations in the rc files.

