In article <1991Jul5.213303.14216@crl.dec.com>, jg@crl.dec.com (Jim Gettys) writes:
> In article <jmn.678748191@power.Berkeley.EDU> jmn@power.berkeley.edu (J. Mark Noworolski) writes:
> >
> >Are the two machines compatible to the extent that I can just unplug the
> >hard disk from the 3100 and plug it in to the 5000 and then boot? Or is it
> >more complicated than that? 
> >
> 
> Make sure you have configured a kernel for both the DS3100 and the DS5000.
> 

	You can with little difficulty configure a kernel that will
	run on both systems.  The two biggest differences are CPU
	specific code and SCSI support.

	For CPU support make sure you have both of these in the
	configuration file:

		cpu		"DS3100"
		cpu		"DS5000"

	For SCSI support borrow from the GENERIC configuration file:

	1.  The DECstation 3100 only has one "ibus" the 5000 has
	    many.

		adapter		ibus0	at nexus?
		adapter		ibus1	at nexus?
		adapter		ibus2	at nexus?
		adapter		ibus3	at nexus?
		adapter		ibus4	at nexus?
		adapter		ibus5	at nexus?
		adapter		ibus6	at nexus?
		adapter		ibus7	at nexus?

	2.  The DECstation 3100 uses the SII for the SCSI controller.
	    The 5000 uses "asc".

		controller	sii0	at ibus?	vector sii_intr
		controller	asc0	at ibus?	vector ascintr
		controller	asc1	at ibus?	vector ascintr
		controller	asc2	at ibus?	vector ascintr
		controller	asc3	at ibus?	vector ascintr

	3.  This part is abbreviated to get the point across.  You'll
	    Either an SII or an ASC, never both.  So for each unit
	    number in the configuration you can duplicate the "disk"
	    and tape lines:

		disk		rz0     at sii0         drive 0
		disk		rz0	at asc0		drive 0

		tape		tz5     at sii0         drive 5
		tape		tz5     at asc0         drive 5

	    Refer to the GENERIC configuration file for others.

	4.  The DECstation 5000 can have extra Ethernet adapters
	    and the FDDI adapter.

		device		ln0	at ibus?	vector lnintr
		device          ln1     at ibus?        vector lnintr
		device          ln2     at ibus?        vector lnintr
		device          ln3     at ibus?        vector lnintr
		device		fza0	at ibus?	vector fzaintr
		device		fza1	at ibus?	vector fzaintr
		device		fza2	at ibus?	vector fzaintr

	5.  The DECstation 5000 has a wider range of graphics subsystems.
	    See what Jim said about different X servers.  Refer to the
	    manual pages for which of these you're interested in.

		device          pm0     at ibus?        vector pmvint
		device          cfb0    at ibus?        vector cfbvint
		device          gq0     at ibus?        vector gqintr
		device          ga0     at ibus?        vector gaintr
-- 
Alan Rollow				alan@nabeth.cxn.dec.com


