	(Much editorial commentary removed)

There are a couple tricks to getting LAT printing under Ultrix.  However,
it's quite doable.

1) I'd recommend not sharing the port between Ultrix and VMS.  Ultrix forgets
to release the port periodically.

2) When you specify the printer's terminal server and port, you can EITHER
specify them in /etc/printcap OR in your lcp line.  Don't do both, it
confuses LAT.

3) Be sure that the ct field in /etc/printcap points to LAT, i.e. ct=lat.

4) Be sure you've got all the baud rates matching.  That seems to help.

5) Be sure your LAT port is set to access remote, break disabled.

6) Be sure the port is set to off in /etc/ttys.

That ought to do it.

