I got rid of the hung port problem when sharing between Ultrix and VMS.
I did three things:

   1) Got the LAT patches from DEC (grr....)

   2) Specified the terminal server and port when LAT is started in rc.local.
      I was using it in printcap but after I got it working the other way
      I didn't to mess with it.  It might work just fine in printcap.

   3) Protected lpd the way it's supposed to be protected.  It should be
      owned by root, group daemon, and protected 6711 (setuid, setgid).
      I think it was 700, owner root, group system in the distribution.

Ports don't hang anymore and the VMS people were especially happy.  A problem
still exists with LAT printing, though.

It happens when VMS already has the port and Ultrix comes along and tries to
open it.  The Ultrix open fails and thinks that the queue is terminally ill
even though the port is just busy.  The daemon dies and has to be restarted
manually.  lpd isn't smart enough (at least the LAT code isn't, anyway) to
realize the port was just busy and to keep trying.  It's also possible that
LAT is returning the wrong error code.  On VMS, if there is a problem accessing
a printer it will keep trying indefinitely.

If I had the source I'd fix it myself.  Unfortunately, our source license
is still in the works.  I've seen the code for the 3.1 lpd and the fix should
be trivial.  All it needs is some code that will continue trying the open
after it fails.  Anyone with 4.x source want to try it?

