We've been having serious hardware problems with 3 of our 4 DECstation
5000/120's and a 5000/200 server since we received them.  To date:

5000/120 monochromes (two of them).
  When shutdown, reboot doesn't work: SCSI bus doesn't seem to "wake
  up", and SCSI drive doesn't boot.  Required reseating the scsi cable
  at two occasions, and another time letting it "rest" overnight
  solved the problem.  

5000/120 color:
  today, after a shutdown and a poweroff, the power to the CPU
  wouldn't go back on, even though it was feeding power (AC) to the
  monitor.  Switching on and off 5 times was needed before a bootup.

5000/200:
  Same SCSI problem as described for the monochrome 120's.  The LED
  lights in the back corresponded (according to DEC hardware support) to
  "Replace System Board".  Luckily, that wasn't needed -- the scsi cable
  was changed and worked fine since.

We can deal with these problems in the first few weeks, but we'd hate
to see them continue throughout the years...  Has anyone else had
these problems?  Do we just have a bad batch of SCSI connectors?  

I'll let our DEC reps know about this, of course.

