> If there is someone out there who has gotten either of these packages to
> work with the Ultrix4.2 uucico, I'd appreciate hearing from you.  All I've
> managed to accomplish is get uucico STTY FAILED ASSERT ERRORs in the ERRLOG.

That's about what I'd expect from previous experience.  The ultrix uucp
checks the result codes from various ioctl()'s it does for the serial lines.
Since these ioctl's are invalid for a network socket, it fails.

A while ago, I patched the vax version to nop out ioctl() and a couple
other goodies and got it to work with the 4.3 BSD uucpd, however what with
the mips executable being stripped and the risc release omitting basic
tools like adb, I don't think it would be easy to repeat the excercise.

