A couple of more minor doc peeves:

It's kind of frustrating when the document format changes.  We've very
consistant about keeping manuals up to date, labelled, and organized.
When the format changes we have to shuffle stuff around and it's no
longer "at your fingertips".  Two failings we've noticed in particular --
some of the newer guides are no longer 3-hole punched, and some change
from 8.5x11 to 5.5x7 (or whatever).

DEC ships your original manual set with binders and spine markers.
When the manuals change (combine), new spine markers should be shipped
and new binders if needed.
