We have a 'dual-headed' II/GPX, so yes it is possible to have two GPX board
sets in a II/GPX.  I have no idea if VMS supports it, but as far as DECwindows
goes, it is actually two separate 'displays' in the sense of an X display.

That is, you run two servers, one for each display, keyboard and mouse.  We
use xdm - here is our server config (xdm/Xservers) file:

:1 Local local /usr/bin/X11/Xqdss :1
:0 Local local /usr/bin/X11/Xqdss :0

