In article <1991Jul15.130750.11759@ohm.york.ac.uk>, pete@ohm.york.ac.uk (-Pete French.) writes:
> What does "installing" mean, how do I set about doing it and how
> difficult is it going to be to keep one of these machines going ?

  Generally it means tying down various mechanical items so they won't
move around (like disk drive heads), losing all the documentation, pil-
fering the power cords, etc.

  If you get the manuals with the system, there is a VAX 750 installation
guide. It details the steps needed for the CPU. Each peripheral will have
a similar manual.

  Be sure to get the little cassette tapes (TU58's) that go in the 750's
drive, or you won't be able to run any tests, etc.

  The 750 has a "maintenance card" (L0006) which is property of DEC. They
may have removed this when they deinstalled the system(s). If so, they
may or may not have moved the cables that need moving when this board
