M920 modules should be removed, replace with G727 module.
M7856 is a DL11-W serial/clock card. Only enable clock on one card. Don't
    change DIP switch settings or configure all cards with identical
    switch settings. Identify standard console serial interface (Address
    777560), set Baud rate and other comm settings. Console must be connected
    to module with standard address.  
Extra serial card on RK611 backplane should be removed. (Never used this
    controller, but Peripherals Handbook 1980 shows the slot as unused).
Check NPG wire wrap jumpers (CA1 to CB1) on backplane. Only remove jumper
    from UNIBUS modules using data transfer without processor intervention
    (Eg. RL controller). If an NPG module is removed from a slot, rejumper
    CA1 to CB1.
Check all power supply voltages (there are two independant +5V supplies).
Maintenance mode for programmer's Console should have cables between M7859
    module and processor card (note: cables crossover).
Check Boot option on Bootstrap/Terminator.
Try to get appropriate documentation. Some examples:
    EK-11034-UG   Systems User's Manual, includes basic troubleshooting.
    EK-RL012-UG   RL01/RL02 User Guide.
    EK-M9312-TM   M9312 Technical Manua.l
    Documentation Products Directory (1984 vintage or similar).
    PDP-11/04, 34A Series Configuring Guide (1980).

If desperate
   Terminate Backplane at M9202 module (replace with M9302).
   Remove Floating Point Unit, etc. Configure with memory, processor,
     front panel, DL11-WM console serial device, and fill all empty connector
     D sockets with a Bus Grant Jumper card (G727).
   Compare with a going system at a local site (impossible for you?). Check
     individual boards in another (going) system. Try local Universities,
     large computer sites, manufacturing sites, local computer clubs or
     amateur radio/electronic clubs as other likely sources of an expert.
   If still dead, remove processor boards and use a PDP-11/04 processor,
     backplanes are interchangeable (first two slots are special and 
     not UNIBUS). 
   Find a local service organization.
   
Goodluck.


