Hi,

We are getting ready to install 3 Fujitsu M2266SA disks on a DEC5400 with
a CMD 223 disk/tape controller. We already have an Exebyte 8200 attached
to the CMD 223 and it has been working for 4 months. We have the CMD 223
disk portion of the controller disabled. The CMD controller is supposed
to make the disks appear to responds as DEC MSCP type devices. It
makes the Exebyte appear as a DEC TMSCP device under Ultrix 4.1 (and
it's tape limitations).

What is a working (good) disktab entry to use for the Fujitsu 1.2 GB
M2266SA disks?

Has anybody had any experience connecting the CMD 223 and Fujutsu
M2266SA disks? Are there any 'non-standard' board settings required
for the CMD 223 such as disabling (hopefully not) synchronous mode?

We have an older Dialog SCSI-MSCP controller with 3 Wren V's and a
Wren VII and they have worked fine, including a stint as the system
boot disk (Wren VII). However, we got the CMD 223 for the Exebyte, and
since it is faster than the Dialog, we decided to use it for the new disks.

